faq:
  - q: "What do I need to get a document notarized?"
    a: "Bring the document unsigned and a valid government-issued photo ID. Everyone who signs needs to be present in person."
  - q: "What is an apostille?"
    a: "An apostille certifies a public or notarized document so it is accepted in another country that is part of the Hague Apostille Convention. We help you prepare documents for apostille."
  - q: "Can a notary give legal advice or prepare my documents?"
    a: "No. A New York notary public who isn't an attorney can't give legal advice or draft legal documents. If you're not sure which form you need, ask the agency or attorney who requested it."
